{
  "schema": "mmt-dpi/resource-bounds-budgets/v1",
  "description": "Reproducible adversarial resource budgets (issue #394, F-PERF-001..004). Every value is a deterministic count or byte total from fixed-seed workloads; no packets-per-second or production timing guarantee is asserted. Checks: eq/le/lt compare `metric` with `limit`, or with `factor` x `limit_metric`; sum requires `metric` to equal the sum of `parts` (every refusal accounted). `baseline` is the reported pre-fix figure a budget improves on (ftp-control's open-visit baselines are the analytical N(N-1)/2 of the former tail walk, not a measurement).",
  "fixtures": {
    "ipv6-hash": {
      "issue": 379,
      "finding": "F-PERF-001",
